---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import IdentityCard from "../components/IdentityCard.astro";
import { loadIdentities } from "../lib/identities.mjs";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-400.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-500.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-800.css";
import "../styles/site.css";

const identities = loadIdentities();

const installCmd = `npx shadcn add https://uiforagents.com/registries/ocean-calm/ocean-calm.json`;
const installConfig = JSON.stringify(
  {
    registries: {
      "@uiforagents": "https://uiforagents.com/registries/{name}/{name}.json",
    },
  },
  null,
  2
);
---
<Base>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">uiforagents</p>
      <h1>Design identities for agent-built apps</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Complete, opinionated design systems on shadcn/ui - tokens, component treatments, blocks,
        fonts, and motion, bundled with the prompt-pack your agent follows. Pick an identity, install
        it with one command, and ship product without making a single design decision.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#identities">Browse identities</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#how">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="identities" aria-label="Identity gallery">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The catalogue</p>
        <h2>Three identities, ready to ship</h2>
        <p>Every card below is live: it carries its identity's own color. Open one for a working demo, install commands, and the agent prompt-pack.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="identity-grid">
        {identities.map((identity) => <IdentityCard {identity} />)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="how" aria-label="How it works">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>From decision to shipped UI in three steps</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h3>Pick an identity</h3>
          <p>Each identity is a complete design system: theme tokens, component treatments, composed blocks, fonts, and motion defaults. The design decisions are already made.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h3>Install with one command</h3>
          <p>Identities are shadcn registry payloads. Add one with a URL, or register the <code>@uiforagents</code> namespace once and install by name.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <h3>Hand your agent the prompt-pack</h3>
          <p>Attach the identity's prompt-pack.md to every agent building UI. It settles typography, color, density, and do/don'ts - the agent stops improvising design and starts shipping.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="install" aria-label="Install">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
        <h2>One command into any shadcn app</h2>
        <p>Tailwind v4 + React 18+. Swap the slug in the URL for any identity in the catalogue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <div>
          <h3>Install by URL</h3>
          <pre class="code-block"><code>{installCmd}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Or register the namespace<span class="hint">components.json</span></h3>
          <pre class="code-block"><code>{installConfig}</code></pre>
          <p class="code-note">Then: <code>npx shadcn add @uiforagents/ocean-calm</code> (any slug works in place of <code>ocean-calm</code>).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="agents" aria-label="For agents">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">For agents</p>
        <h2>The prompt-pack is the integration</h2>
        <p>Humans pick the identity; agents build with it. Two artifacts make that work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spec-grid">
        <div class="spec-card">
          <h3>Agent prompt-pack</h3>
          <p class="desc" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);">A markdown contract attached to every agent building UI: fonts, color rules, density, spacing, motion, and do/don'ts. It is the difference between "make it look nice" and a premium result.</p>
          <a href="/prompt-packs/ocean-calm.md">Read the ocean-calm pack raw →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <h3>shadcn registry payload</h3>
          <p class="desc" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);">The machine-readable surface the shadcn CLI consumes: theme CSS, overrides, and composed blocks in one validated payload.</p>
          <a href="/registries/ocean-calm/ocean-calm.json">Inspect the registry payload →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card">
          <h3>Identity spec</h3>
          <p class="desc" style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);">identity.json is the source of record: tokens, block list, tested versions, license. Published as JSON for tooling.</p>
          <a href="/identities/ocean-calm.json">Fetch the identity spec →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
